#
# Counter-example for the reasoned-graph math: expression-identity gate
# (crates/logic/src/math_expression.rs, check_surface_leak_in_normal_form): ex:src is
# the math:normalizes source of a math:NormalizationDeclaration and directly carries
# math:rendersAs — a surface-stratum (rendered) predicate leaking into a computation
# that must stay structural. The gate MUST raise math:SurfaceLeakInNormalForm (and
# neither of its two siblings math:StructuralKeyDrift /
# math:StructuralKeyOnRejectedExpression).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:decl a math:NormalizationDeclaration ;
    math:normalizes ex:src ;
    math:normalizesTo ex:tgt .

ex:src a math:NumberLiteral ;
    math:literalValue 1 ;
    math:rendersAs ex:rendered .

ex:tgt a math:NumberLiteral ;
    math:literalValue 1 .
